          "For usage report, the governing source is the onboarding tracker; a note in the queue is only a pointer to that source. For recurring usage report work, use the same QBR packet type and the same field labels so a sample can be compared across owners. Use a separate reason code for conflicting evidence so the pattern can be reviewed without reading every message. A source that cannot be opened by the reviewer is not a usable source, even if the operator can see it on their screen.",
          "Do not treat a forwarded email as the record itself when the governing value lives in the support desk; the email may explain intent, but it does not replace the field. A escalation record that arrives after the action can still be useful, but it must be marked late and linked to the correction it supports. If the support desk and the escalation record disagree, stop the dependent action and record both values with the time each was observed. A late escalation record is still evidence, but it should not be presented as if it existed at the time of the first decision."
